 "details": {
  "title": "The Very Thought of You, on the Fret Finder guitar",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Stacey Kent’s live record brought down to A-flat: concert C4 to E-flat 5 (D to F for the trumpet). The notes are the lead sheet’s; each sits where she sings it, so the time is hers, rubato, and the long notes last as long as she holds them. The intro and the piano solo are the guitar’s: the trumpet rests. After the solo she sings the second half again and holds the last A-flat.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Ray Noble (1934)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, placed on the singer’s timing from the record"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "A-flat major concert (B-flat for the trumpet)"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro (guitar), the song, piano solo (guitar), the second half again, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (tvt-guitar.mp3), 4:33"
   ]
  ]
 }
